      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I understand the test. Let me write an improved version with better understandability: removing dead code, unused imports/fields/helpers, and clarifying the intent of each assertion step.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all dead code (unused imports, `LOG`/`log` methods, `BAD_ENCODING_NAME`, `allocate`, `getByteBufferUtf8`, `checkDecodeHex*` helpers), renames the sanity-check method to `isCharsetSane` for clarity, and replaces the terse numbered comments with descriptive section headers and assertion messages that explain *why* each check is being made."
